.o-generic-modal
  h1.o-generic-modal__title NEJM Weekly CME Program
  .f-body--sm
    .m-certif
      .m-certif-message
        span.m-certif-legend.f-caps CME Certificate
        h3.m-certif-congrats.f-caps Congratulations!
        p
          span.m-certif-intro The Massachusetts Medical Society certifies that
          span.m-certif-name.f-h3 Marius Roosendaal
          |  has participated in the enduring material, titled the NEJM Weekly CME Program on 7/4/2017, this activity is designated for 
          strong 1.0 AMA PRA Category 1 Credits™
          | . The Massachusetts Medical Society is accredited by the Accreditation Council for Continuing Medical Education to provide continuing medical education for physicians.
        .m-certif-exam
          p.m-certif-examType.f-caps Case records of The Massachusetts General Hospital
          h1.m-certif-examTitle.f-h5 Case 10-2017 — Subclinical Hypothyroidism
          p.f-author
            | Robin P. Peeters, M.D., Ph.D. 
            span.m-certif-examCitation N Engl J Med 2017;  376:2556-2565
      p.m-certif-footer.f-related
        | You can print this page as a confirmation of your completion of this program. We will also e-mail you a confirmation notice for your records and the credit will be stored in your profile which can be accessed and printed at any time.
        | Thank you for your participation in the NEJM CME Program. Please provide us feedback by completing the 
        a(href='#', data-behavior='OpenInModal') Exam Evaluation
        | .
        br
        |         The 
        i New England Journal of Medicine
        |  is a publication of NEJM Group,
        | a division of the Massachusetts Medical Society.
.g-modal__actions
  a(href='#', target='_blank')
    svg.icon--print(aria-label='Print')
      use(xmlns:xlink='http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink', xlink:href='#icon--print')
